"slick-slide00\" aria-label=\"1 of 1\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-selected=\"true\">1</button></li></ul></div><!-- event slideshow -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t</div><!-- top row -->\t\n\n\t<div class=\"top-row bg-white\" style=\"position: relative;\">\n\t\t<div class=\"row-wrap\">\n\n\t\t\t<div class=\"term-flag\" style=\"background:#00ADDA ;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span>Film</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div class=\"flex d-flex row\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-md-8 pl-80 pr-60 px-sm-0 col-sm-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h1>All that Glitters – Community Screening and Q&amp;A</h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Ryan a hapless romantic enlists the ghost of Shakespeare to help get the role of Romeo in the school play and win over his Juliet.</h3>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><p>All That Glitters is a heartfelt coming-of-age comedy romance about Ryan, a teenage boy struggling to find his place at school and at home with his father, who also happens to be his English teacher. After a heated argument, Ryan conjures the ghost of Shakespeare and gets a chance to step into the spotlight, win the girl he admires, and finally be seen.</p>\n<p>What begins as a playful, fish-out-of-water adventure becomes a poignant story about love, loss, and the universal desire to belong.</p>\n<p>Post-Screening Q&amp;A with Peter Lavery (writer/director) Joe Andrews (Producer) and Mark Lavery (actor)</p>\n</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p style=\"color: #00ADDA;\"></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"back-link\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a style=\"color: #00ADDA;\" href=\"/whats-on/\"><strong>Back to listings</strong></a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t</div><!-- col end -->\n\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-12 mt-sm-30\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"single-event-details\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Wed 02 December 2026</strong>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">FIlm Starts 7.30pm</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Tickets: £10</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"event-button arrow-button arrow-right \">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a style=\"background: #00ADDA;\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.ticketsolve.com/ticketbooth/shows/1173694118\">Buy Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div><!-- col end -->\n\t\t\t</div>\n\n\n\n\t\t</div><!-- row wrap -->\n\t</div><!-- top row -->\n\n\t<div class=\"bottom-row\">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"row-wrap\">\n\n\n\t\t\t<div class=\"event_content_box_wrap\"><div style=\"background:#00ADDA;\" class=\"white-text  event_content_box colour_box\"><h3><strong>About the Film</strong></h3>\n<p>After a heated argument with his father, Ryan’s frustration and loneliness reach a tipping point. Alone with a copy of Hamlet, he accidentally summons the ghost of William Shakespeare himself. Eccentric, chaotic, and bewildered by the modern world, Shakespeare becomes Ryan’s unlikely mentor. He first helps Ryan with homework and then guides him toward a far greater challenge: stepping out of the shadows to play Romeo after the school’s effortlessly popular, Hugo, drops out of the production.</p>\n<p>Under Shakespeare’s guidance, Ryan gains confidence, discovers his own voice, and learns the strange courage that comes from being truly seen both on stage and in life. Along the way, he navigates complicated friendships, awkward encounters with Jasmine, and the messy dynamics of growing up, realizing that love is not just about winning someone’s heart but about accepting himself and allowing others to see him.</p>\n<p>By the play’s climax, Ryan faces choices that test his newfound maturity. With guidance from Shakespeare and the support of his loyal friend Cassie, he reconciles with his father, embraces his individuality, and discovers the rewards of honesty, courage, and true connection.</p>\n<p>Blending contemporary teenage awkwardness with timeless themes of love, loss, and self-expression, All That Glitters reimagines Shakespeare for a modern audience. With wit and warmth, it celebrates the luminous, chaotic, and transformative journey of growing up, showing that even the most ordinary lives can take centre stage.</p>\n<p><div class=\"video-placeholder-youtube\" data-cky-tag=\"video-placeholder\" id=\"ZrWHxaHA\" style=\"width: 640px; height: 360px; background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(76, 72, 72, 0.7), rgba(76, 72, 72, 0.7)), url(&quot;https://img.youtube.com/vi/tS8mcM4bz4k/maxresdefault.jpg&quot;);\"><p class=\"video-placeholder-text-youtube\" data-cky-tag=\"placeholder-title\" style=\"display: none;\">[cky_video_placeholder_title]</p></div></p>\n</div></div>\n\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"event-button arrow-button arrow-right \" style=\"margin-top: 20px;float: right\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a style=\"background: #00ADDA;\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://irishculturalcentre.ticketsolve.com/ticketbooth/shows/1173694118\">Buy Tickets</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t</div><!-- row wrap -->\t\n\t</div><!-- bottom row -->\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"suggested-row\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"row-wrap\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"pill\" style=\"background: #00ADDA\">\n\t\t\t\t\tInterested in\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFilm?\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t<h3>You may also like</h3>\n\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"suggested-cards slick-initialized slick-slider\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"pull-left suggested-left slick-arrow slick-disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"><span class=\"icon-arrow-left\"></span></button>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"slick-list draggable\"><div class=\"slick-track\" style=\"opacity: 1; width: 3366px; transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px);\"><div class=\"slide slick-slide slick-current slick-active\" data-slick-index=\"0\" aria-hidden=\"false\" style=\"width: 354px;\" tabindex=\"0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n<div class=\"suggested-card\">\n    <div class=\"suggested-card__image\">\n        <img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://irishculturalcentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/istockphoto-1082906740-612x612